  "author_association": "NONE",
  "body": "I'm trying to wrap my head around this paper, and one thing I find confusing in the reference repo is how ACT is only active [during training](https://github.com/sapientinc/HRM/blob/171e2fcde636bcb7e6c0073a9983ed5252f04753/models/hrm/hrm_act_v1.py#L265). Doesn't that negative the purpose of having adaptive compute during inference time, and isn't what you want to show that it learns to stop reasoning during inference when further reasoning won't further improve the result?",
